# Baia Swimwear — Cursor AI Context

## Project Overview

Baia Swimwear is a bilingual (Hebrew/English) e-commerce platform for premium swimwear.
Monorepo managed by **pnpm 9** workspaces.

## Tech Stack

| Layer       | Technology                          |
|-------------|-------------------------------------|
| Client      | Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19  |
| Server      | NestJS 11                           |
| Database    | PostgreSQL 16, Prisma 6 ORM        |
| Auth        | better-auth (session cookies)       |
| Styling     | Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui         |
| State       | Zustand (cart), server data via fetch |
| Storage     | S3 (LocalStack dev, any S3-compat prod) via Upload entity |
| i18n        | next-intl, RTL support for Hebrew  |
| Monorepo    | pnpm workspaces                     |

## Monorepo Structure

```
baia/
├── apps/client/          # Next.js storefront + admin panel (port 3000)
├── apps/server/          # NestJS REST API (port 8000)
├── packages/shared/      # Zod schemas, shared TypeScript types
├── scripts/              # Migration & init scripts
├── docs/                 # SPEC.md, ADRs
└── CONTEXT.md            # Domain glossary
```

## Authentication

- **NOT JWT** — uses better-auth with HTTP-only session cookies (prefix: `baia`)
- Roles: `ADMIN` | `CUSTOMER` (Prisma enum on User model)
- Admin guard: `@UseGuards(AuthGuard) @Roles('ADMIN')` on NestJS routes
- Client admin guard: server layout fetches `/api/auth/get-session`, redirects if not ADMIN
- Auth routes: `/api/auth/*` (mounted before NestJS `/v1` prefix)

## API Conventions

- Global prefix: `/v1`
- Public routes: `/v1/products`, `/v1/categories`, `/v1/cart`, etc.
- Auth-required: `/v1/orders/my`, `/v1/wishlist`
- Admin routes: `/v1/admin/products`, `/v1/admin/categories`, `/v1/admin/orders`, `/v1/admin/analytics`, `/v1/admin/uploads`, `/v1/admin/site-config`
- Guards applied per-route (no global guard)
- No DTO classes — inline TypeScript types in controllers

## Database Schema (Key Models)

- `User` — better-auth managed, has `role` (ADMIN/CUSTOMER)
- `Category` — self-referencing hierarchy via `parentId`, bilingual names, `imageUploadId` -> Upload
- `Product` — bilingual name/description, basePrice, categoryId, isFeatured, isActive
- `ProductVariant` — color, size, sku, stockQuantity, priceOverride, salePrice with date range
- `ProductImage` — linked to Product, has `uploadId` -> Upload for S3, legacy `url` field
- `Upload` — single source of truth for all S3 files (s3Key, s3Bucket, mimeType, sizeBytes, fileName)
- `Cart` / `CartItem` — guest (sessionId) or authenticated (userId)
- `Order` / `OrderItem` — full order lifecycle with status enum
- `Coupon` — percentage or fixed discount with rules
- `SiteConfig` — singleton for shipping, hero banner, `heroImageUploadId` -> Upload

## Storage Architecture

- `StorageService` interface: `upload(file, key, mimeType)`, `delete(key)`, `getUrl(key)`
- `S3StorageService` — production/dev implementation using @aws-sdk/client-s3
- `LocalStorageService` — legacy fallback writing to `./uploads/`
- Switch via `STORAGE_PROVIDER` env var (`s3` or `local`)
- `Upload` entity tracks every file in S3 (s3Key, bucket, metadata)
- S3 key structure: `products/{productId}/{uploadId}.{ext}`, `categories/{categoryId}/{uploadId}.{ext}`, `site/{uploadId}.{ext}`
- Dev: LocalStack S3 at localhost:4566, bucket `baia-assets`
- Prod: any S3-compatible provider (AWS, R2, B2)

## Environment Variables (Server)

```
PORT=8000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://baia:baia@localhost:5433/baia
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=<secret>
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8000
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:3000
STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3          # s3 | local
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566
S3_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:4566
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_ACCESS_KEY=test
S3_SECRET_KEY=test
S3_BUCKET=baia-assets
```

## Environment Variables (Client)

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8000
```

## Client Routing

- `/{locale}/` — storefront (header + footer)
- `/{locale}/admin/` — admin panel (AdminShell sidebar)
- `/{locale}/login`, `/{locale}/register` — standalone auth pages
- Locales: `he` (default, RTL), `en` (LTR)

## Coding Conventions

- Server: NestJS modules per domain, services inject PrismaService and STORAGE_SERVICE
- Client: `'use client'` for interactive admin pages, server components for layouts
- Bilingual fields: `nameHe`/`nameEn`, `descriptionHe`/`descriptionEn`
- Prices: Prisma Decimal(10,2), converted to number in API responses
- IDs: cuid() for all models
- Slugs: unique, URL-safe identifiers for products and categories
